<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="6fea584f">&lt;p&gt;
    Evaluating training is done by creating a feedback mechanism to capture information from those trained.&amp;nbsp; A clear
    process to provide and receive feedback is set.&amp;nbsp; Questions revolve around well-defined metrics to provide clear
    results.&amp;nbsp; In line with the training strategy and organizational goals and objectives, evaluating training can be
    as simple as determining if the participants liked a training module to as complex as determining the direct
    organizational ROI of a training intervention.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Create learning evaluation measures and process. Evaluating training is often multi-faceted and may vary from
    project-to-project. General guidelines for evaluating training is as follows:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Evaluate the training effectiveness using agreed mechanisms (e.g., surveys, examinations, feedback forms,
        instructor observational assessments
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine whether any participants require monitoring or further support/training as they start implementing the
        training in their operational environment
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Note which points needs to be monitored in the 4-6 week evaluation and 3 month evaluation
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Implement the agreed post-training evaluation mechanisms to monitor the effectiveness of the training.&amp;nbsp;
        Possible ways of doing this include: surveys observational assessments, focus groups, workshops, etc
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Use the observations from the on-the-day evaluation to check any trouble areas or trainees who required additional
        support
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Learners assess training by rating perceived value, relevance of content, delivery method effectiveness and other
    metrics defined for the change initiative.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
